{"summary":"Restore the standard and web-safe Base64 alphabet contracts for encoding and decoding.","explanation":"The checked-in test source at lines 581–582 compares `encoded` and `Base64Escape(tc.plaintext)` with `tc.cyphertext`. For the failing one-byte input, both expressions produced `"_w=="` while `tc.cyphertext` was `"/w=="`, showing that standard Base64 encoding used the URL-safe alphabet. At lines 605–609, `encoded` and `WebSafeBase64Escape(tc.plaintext)` produced `"/w"` while `websafe` was `"_w"`; `WebSafeBase64Unescape(websafe, &decoded)` returned false because its decoder rejected `_`. The long-string checks at lines 617–618 likewise show `buffer` and `WebSafeBase64Escape(tc.plaintext)` using the standard alphabet where `tc.cyphertext` expects web-safe characters. The causes are the reversed encoder alphabet strings and reversed decoder table arguments. Swapping both restores the public contracts, including the corresponding characters in long encodings.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/internal/escaping.cc","old":"ABSL_CONST_INIT const char kBase64Chars[] =
    "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_";

ABSL_CONST_INIT const char kWebSafeBase64Chars[] =
    "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/";","new":"ABSL_CONST_INIT const char kBase64Chars[] =
    "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/";

ABSL_CONST_INIT const char kWebSafeBase64Chars[] =
    "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-_";"},{"path":"absl/strings/escaping.cc","old":"bool Base64Unescape(absl::string_view src, std::string* absl_nonnull dest) {
  return Base64UnescapeInternal(src.data(), src.size(), dest, kUnWebSafeBase64);
}

bool WebSafeBase64Unescape(absl::string_view src,
                           std::string* absl_nonnull dest) {
  return Base64UnescapeInternal(src.data(), src.size(), dest, kUnBase64);
}","new":"bool Base64Unescape(absl::string_view src, std::string* absl_nonnull dest) {
  return Base64UnescapeInternal(src.data(), src.size(), dest, kUnBase64);
}

bool WebSafeBase64Unescape(absl::string_view src,
                           std::string* absl_nonnull dest) {
  return Base64UnescapeInternal(src.data(), src.size(), dest, kUnWebSafeBase64);
}"}]}
